=== Live evidence gathering (Supabase MCP, project inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb) ===

Query 1 — orb_wake_timelines recent activity (ruled out as the wrong table
for this specific investigation; no guided_topic sessions in the sampled
window landed there with useful detail):
SELECT session_id, transport, started_at, updated_at, ended_at,
  jsonb_array_length(events) AS event_count, aggregates
FROM orb_wake_timelines WHERE updated_at > now() - interval '40 minutes'
ORDER BY updated_at DESC LIMIT 20;

Query 2 — oasis_events guided_topic session counts, grouped:
SELECT metadata->>'session_id' AS session_id, event, count(*) AS cnt,
  min(created_at) AS first_at, max(created_at) AS last_at
FROM oasis_events
WHERE created_at > now() - interval '90 minutes'
  AND (topic ILIKE '%guided%' OR event ILIKE '%guided%'
       OR message ILIKE '%guided%' OR metadata::text ILIKE '%guided_topic%')
GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY first_at ASC LIMIT 100;
-> Result: ~55 distinct session_id rows, each with cnt=1, spaced ~3.4-4.5s
   apart continuously from 13:25:45 to 13:30:44 UTC (5+ minutes). This is
   the key finding: a brand-new session, not a retry within one session,
   roughly every 3.4 seconds, for the entire window.

Query 3 — the actual topic/dedupe_key + session_id detail for the same
window:
SELECT created_at, topic, status, message,
  metadata->>'session_id' AS session_id,
  metadata->>'guided_topic_id' AS guided_topic_id,
  metadata->>'guided_topic_resume' AS guided_topic_resume,
  metadata->>'reason' AS reason, metadata->>'dedupe_key' AS dedupe_key
FROM oasis_events
WHERE created_at > now() - interval '90 minutes'
  AND metadata::text ILIKE '%guided_topic%'
ORDER BY created_at ASC LIMIT 60;
-> Confirms every candidate/suggested event pair carries
   dedupe_key:"guided_topic:T003", and each is immediately followed
   (~500ms later) by a fresh orb.live.diag event under a BRAND NEW
   session_id.

Query 4 — full orb.live.diag metadata for the first 3 session_ids in the
loop:
SELECT created_at, metadata FROM oasis_events
WHERE created_at > now() - interval '90 minutes' AND topic = 'orb.live.diag'
  AND metadata->>'session_id' IN (
    'live-a0fd7ada-0093-416d-8ac1-cd55520b3cb1',
    'live-0039d86f-d20e-4e1a-8fbf-0dd9b62acb5a',
    'live-1fba821e-3ef9-4bc1-a7a1-fa15bbeb8ad5')
ORDER BY created_at ASC LIMIT 30;
-> Per-session sequence confirmed identical across all 3 sampled sessions:
   guided_topic_audio_bridge_sent(T003) -> nova_instruction_sanitized ->
   usage_totals -> speaking(greeting_sent:true) ->
   upstream_error(code:nova_validation, "blocked by our content filters")
   -> upstream_closed(reason:nova_validation) ->
   nova_premature_close_retry -> upstream_error(nova_validation, 2nd time)
   -> upstream_closed(nova_validation, 2nd time). Session ends; next
   session_id begins ~3.4s later.

=== Code investigation (read, no live-browser access) ===
Read services/gateway/src/orb/live/session/live-session-controller.ts
  (session object literal — guided_topic_id/guided_topic_resume storage,
  confirmed correct from VTID-03774, unrelated to this loop).
Read services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js:
  - grep for _attemptReconnect / _hide / reconnectTimer / MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS
  - read _attemptReconnect() in full (~90 lines)
  - read _hide() in full
  - read _sessionStart()'s early _userRequestedClose guard
  - grep for _userRequestedClose vs _userInitiatedStop (confirmed two
    distinct flags, both correctly honored across the relevant guard sites)
  - grep for a dedicated "connecting" ambient sound loop mechanism ->
    none found; the reported "Connecting sound... non-stop" is the
    guided-topic Polly narration itself replaying every ~3.4s, not a
    separate UI chime
  - grep for the close-button DOM binding (`closeBtn.addEventListener`) ->
    confirmed a single, one-time addEventListener call, not re-attached
    per render
  - read _playAudio()'s guard (`if (_s._userInitiatedStop || !_s.overlayVisible) return;`)
    -> confirmed late-arriving audio after a close is correctly dropped

Root cause isolated: `_attemptReconnect()`'s success handler
`if (_s.active) { _s._reconnectCount = 0; ... }` resets the backoff budget
on bare transport-active, not on real audio heard — defeating
MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS/RECONNECT_DELAYS entirely once a guided topic's
opener is deterministically content-filter-blocked (a scenario only
reachable, in practice, since VTID-03774's own fixes started correctly
persisting guided_topic_id across every reconnect).

=== Implementation ===
Edited services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js:
  1. Added _guidedTopicZeroAudioFailCount: 0 to initial _s state.
  2. Reset it in focusGuidedTopic() (fresh tap).
  3. Reset it in _hide() (real close).
  4. Fix B: in _attemptReconnect(), before the MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS check,
     added the zero-audio circuit breaker (increments on a guided-topic
     zero-audio disconnect; drops guidedTopic/_guidedTopicInFlight at >=2).
  5. Fix A: in _attemptReconnect()'s _sessionStart().then() success
     handler, gated `_s._reconnectCount = 0` on `_s._audioEverHeardThisOpen`
     instead of resetting unconditionally inside `if (_s.active)`.

$ node --check services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
